{"type": "model", "t_ms": 65251, "ts": 1795287833.8751118, "turn": 2, "prompt_tokens": 3120, "completion_tokens": 2756, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning_tokens": null, "ttft_ms": 4497, "latency_ms": 62644, "usage_source": "reported", "cache_hit_tokens": null, "cache_miss_tokens": null, "error": "", "text": "{\"thought\": \"The three moduli share factors: n1=pq, n2=pr, n3=qr. I can recover p,q,r via gcd, then factor each modulus and use CRT to recover the flag. Let me write a solver.\", \"action\": \"python\", \"code\": \"import math\\nfrom Crypto.Util.number import long_to_bytes\\n\\\\\\\\ne=65537\\\\n\\np=math.gcd(n1,n2)\\nr=n2//p\\nq=n1//p\\nprint('p,q,r found', p==math.gcd(n1,n3) or True)\\n\\n# recover m from each modulus\\nres=[]\\nfor n, a, b in [(n1,p,q),(n2,p,r),(n3,q,r)]:\\n    phi=(a-1)*(b-1)\\n    d=pow(e,-1,phi)\\n    m=pow(c,d,n)\\n    res.append((m,n))\\n\\n# CRT\\nM=res[0][1]*res[1][1]*res[2][1]\\nans=0\\nfor m,n in res:\\n    Mi=M//n\\n    ans+=m*Mi*pow(Mi,-1,n)\\nans%=M\\nprint(long_to_bytes(ans))\"}"}
